	(text "DC jack overvoltage protection, after D1 (D1 blocks reverse polarity).\nU7 switches off above 1.2 V x (1 + R20/R21) = 5.9 V typ (5.7-6.1 V),\nso a 9-24 V supply on J1 just doesn't power the board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e829cef9-3930-48b4-b6cd-15c3da8d2e69")
	)
	(text "Changes for V6.1\nUse JST-XH-5 horizontal footprint on accessory header.  Rotates pin connections to other boards.\nTBD: SMT caps\nTBD: SMT diode\n\nChanges for v5 --> v6:\nNew accessory JST header (in prep for cable to payphone coin relay board.\nNew i2c gpio chip to handle line2 SHK/RM/FR/PD so we can run uSD AND line 2 AND 4 GPIOs\n4 GPIO header now becomes a JST with power & gnd.\n3.6V or 3.7V regulator for bluetooth module instead of 3.3V.  Also improves headroom for 6V supply?\nFixes:\nMajor bug:  Cheap ESP32 wide footprint had one of the 5V pins shorted to ground. Fixed in this release.\nmove passives in ag1171 footprint area for ag1171 real module... V5 touches caps.\nbigger esp32 holes!  they're a little tight\nTBD:\nDo we want to do SMT 470uF caps?  (add pads) - not now.\n\n\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 169.418 40.386 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f9d54e25-3c7c-4dae-a021-958f86873fa7")
	)
